+\paragraph{Class-A examples.}
+Steady Euler balance gives
+\begin{align}
+    \frac{1}{\rhoEff}\frac{dp}{dr}
+    =
+    \frac{v_\theta^2}{r}.
+\end{align}
+Under \(p\to\lambda p\), the acceleration is invariant.  Likewise a
+transverse wave speed
+\begin{align}
+    c_T^2=\frac{K_T}{\rhoEff}
+\end{align}
+is invariant when \(K_T\to\lambda K_T\).  Rotation curves and propagation
+speeds therefore do not determine the absolute response coefficient.
+
+\paragraph{Class-B no-go for source-free quadratic fields.}
+For
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal L
+    =
+    \frac12\rhoEff|\partial_t\mathbf A|^2
+    -
+    \frac12K|\nabla\times\mathbf A|^2,
+\end{align}
+the simultaneous transformation
+\begin{align}
+    \mathbf A\to s\mathbf A,
+    \qquad
+    \rhoEff\to s^{-2}\rhoEff,
+    \qquad
+    K\to s^{-2}K
+\end{align}
+leaves the action unchanged.  Source-free dispersion, polarization, and
+flux ratios determine only \(K/\rhoEff\).  The EM/torsion sector therefore
+cannot fix \(\rhoEff\) without an independently normalized source or
+detector coupling.
+
+\paragraph{Class-C and class-Q candidates.}
+Absolute pressure differences, boundary forces, Pauli-barrier amplitudes,
+dark-sector pressure amplitudes, mechanical impedances, and resolved
+kinetic energies scale with \(\rhoEff\) and are class-C candidates.  The
+absolute action scale, zero-point fluctuations, thermal noise, and
+correlation amplitudes are class-Q candidates.  In the current Canon,
+however, each such candidate either uses the legacy value \(\rhoRef\),
+contains another unfixed coupling or geometry factor, or lacks an
+independent measurement map.  No validated class-C or class-Q observable
+currently pins \(\rhoEff\).
